This choice matches the most restrictive real dependency this project
relies on at runtime (see below) rather than granting broader rights than
the overall system can actually support. Non-commercial academic/research
use is fully covered.

## Why the whole system is non-commercial-only

This project orchestrates fourteen external tools, each with its own
license, invoked as separate processes (never statically/dynamically
linked into this project's own code), never redistributed as part of this
repository:

- **BepiPred-3.0** (UberClifford/BepiPred-3.0): free for academic
  non-commercial use only; for-profit use requires a separate license
  (contact Morten Nielsen, morni@dtu.dk). Non-commercial only.
- **EpiDope** (mcollatz/EpiDope): MIT.
- **DiscoTope-3.0** (Magnushhoie/DiscoTope-3.0): CC BY-NC 4.0. Non-commercial
  only.
- **ScanNet** (jertubiana/ScanNet): Apache-2.0.
- **TMbed** (BernhoferM/TMbed): Apache-2.0.
- **BLAST+** (NCBI): public domain / U.S. Government work (NCBI-PD).
- **AlgPred2** (Raghava group, IIIT-Delhi): free for scientific use.
  Non-commercial only.
- **StackGlyEmbed** (nafcoder/StackGlyEmbed): no LICENSE file in the code
  repository; its associated paper (Nafi & Rahman, 2025, Bioinformatics
  Advances) is published CC BY 4.0. No explicit code license grant found —
  treated as unconfirmed, not folded into either bucket.
- **NetMHCIIpan-4.3** (DTU Health Tech): academic users only, from publicly
  funded academic/education/research institutions; commercial use requires
  a separate license. Non-commercial only.
- **NetMHCpan-4.2** (DTU Health Tech): same terms as NetMHCIIpan-4.3.
  Non-commercial only.
- **NetCleave** (BSC-CNS-EAPM/NetCleave, fork of pepamengual/NetCleave): no
  LICENSE file in the code repository; its associated paper
  (Amengual-Rigo & Guallar, 2021, Scientific Reports) is published CC BY
  4.0. No explicit code license grant found — treated as unconfirmed, not
  folded into either bucket.
- **IApred** (sebamiles/IAPred): MIT.
- **ToxinPred2** (Raghava group, IIIT-Delhi): free for scientific use.
  Non-commercial only.
- **SignalP-6.0** (DTU Health Tech): academic users only; commercial use is
  a separately licensed, paid tier. Non-commercial only.

None of the above are distributed as part of this repository -- each is
installed independently by whoever sets up this pipeline, per `README.md`.
This LICENSE file covers only the code actually committed here.

**This is not formal legal advice.** If you intend to use this pipeline
or its outputs beyond non-commercial research/academic purposes, verify
the current license terms of each dependency above directly.
